  "instruction": "3D Model Attachment with JEP95 Body Heights\n\n/home/user/Desktop/footprints.pretty/ is a KiCad footprint library containing 12 SOIC, QFP, and LQFP packages with no 3D models attached. /home/user/Desktop/models/ holds the matching.wrl files. /home/user/Desktop/packages.csv maps each footprint to its.wrl filename, JEP95 body height, and intended board side.\n\nOpen the library footprints in KiCad Footprint Editor. Attach the correct.wrl to each footprint so the 3D body sits flush on the board top or bottom with standard KiCad offset, scale, and rotation fields. After updating the library, export the representative footprint `QFP-48_7x7mm_P0.5mm` as an SVG from KiCad.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Write /home/user/Desktop/footprints.pretty/ containing all 12.kicad_mod files.\n2. Each.kicad_mod has exactly one (model...) block referencing its.wrl; the model path must contain the filename listed in /home/user/Desktop/packages.csv.\n3. Use (offset (xyz 0 0 Z)) where Z equals body_height_mm / 2, so the 3D body center sits half its height above the board surface.\n4. Use (scale (xyz 1 1 1)).\n5. Use (rotate (xyz 0 Y 0)) with Y = 180 for layer B.Cu footprints and Y = 0 for F.Cu footprints.\n6. Export `/home/user/Desktop/QFP-48_7x7mm_P0.5mm.svg` from the updated footprint library.\n7. All other footprint content should remain unchanged.\n\nWrite /home/user/Desktop/footprints.pretty/ and /home/user/Desktop/QFP-48_7x7mm_P0.5mm.svg.",
  "source": "KiCad 9 Official Documentation — Footprint Editor / 3D Viewer / Footprint SVG Export, JEDEC JEP95 Registered Package Outlines",
